{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0904"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c076): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c076.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0904"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge film-media/film","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/film-media__film.g4.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",50],["-","five"],["+","six"],["=",685],["+","**John Carpenter** (born 1948) is the master of low-budget suspense, who usually writes and even composes the music for his own films. “Halloween” (1978) made the masked killer Michael Myers the model for a whole wave of slasher films, “Escape from New York” (1981) sent Kurt Russell into a Manhattan turned into a prison, and “The Thing” (1982) trapped a research team in Antarctica with a shape-shifting alien. Like Hitchcock, he slips into his own films in tiny cameos, often only as a voice: in “Halloween” he speaks the telephone voice of Paul, the boyfriend of the babysitter Annie.\n\n"],["=",270],["+","John Carpenter | Halloween, Escape from New York, The Thing |\n| "],["=",23]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",50],["-","fünf"],["+","sechs"],["=",659],["+","**John Carpenter** (geb. 1948) ist der Meister der Spannung mit kleinem Budget, der seine Filme meist selbst schreibt und sogar die Musik dazu komponiert. „Halloween – Die Nacht des Grauens“ (1978) machte den maskierten Mörder Michael Myers zum Vorbild einer ganzen Welle von Slasherfilmen, „Die Klapperschlange“ (1981) schickte Kurt Russell in ein zum Gefängnis gewordenes Manhattan, und „Das Ding aus einer anderen Welt“ (1982) sperrte ein Forschungsteam in der Antarktis mit einem gestaltwandelnden Außerirdischen ein. Wie Hitchcock schleicht er sich in winzigen Cameos in seine eigenen Filme, oft nur als Stimme: In „Halloween“ spricht er am Telefon Paul, den Freund der Babysitterin Annie.\n\n"],["=",266],["+","John Carpenter | Halloween, Die Klapperschlange, Das Ding aus einer anderen Welt |\n| "],["=",23]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0904"},"reason":"a0904 body: Gilliam \"the only American in the group\" → \"the only member born in the United States\" (he gave up US citizenship in 2006); Ridley Scott \"trained as a set designer at the Royal College of Art\" → \"studied at the Royal College of Art, began in television as a set designer\"; cameo sentence now names John Carpenter — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridley_Scott","by":"enrich batch 053","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a0724-a0916.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ridley_Scott"}]},
